cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the integrated report and the individual study reports under studies/."
title: "SUCCES on Bilibili: pre-registered measurement and association studies on Chinese knowledge videos"
abstract: >-
  Three independent studies that share one rule-based codebook and the rule
  "fix the measurement before looking at results". The preceding SC_ study
  pre-registers six directional hypotheses on 64 self-collected videos, runs
  two rounds of blind double coding, and drops the subjective semantic items
  before any model is fitted; its main model is never run. The main SK_ study
  ports the same codebook to two licensed Kaggle datasets (5,717 and 962
  videos) and, after pre-registration, finds 1 / 6 supported hypotheses
  (Concrete, beta = +0.0891, q = 0.0292), an association that depends on
  account-level controls and is not replicated in a second domain. The SW_
  follow-up moves to top-liked comments and finds 0 / 6 on a reproducible
  information-discussion proxy. The studies are not pooled. All statements
  are associational; no causal or "SUCCES works / does not work" claim is made.
authors:
  - name: "SUCCES on Bilibili study"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fsq1815/succes_research"
